.TH pvc-convert-units 1  "pvc-convert-units " 
.SH NAME
pvc\-convert\-units \- Convert amplitude, decibel, Hz, and pitch units
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpvc\-convert\-units\fR <\fB\-\-from\fR> <\fB\-\-to\fR> [\fB\-\-norm\fR] <\fB\-\-value\fR> [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Convert between amplitude/decibel and Hz/octave.pitchclass units.
.PP
Replaces the four standalone unit\-conversion utilities `amptodB`, `dBtoamp`, `Hztopitch`, `pitchtoHz` (`legacy/pvc_src/*.c`) with one command taking a `\-\-from`/`\-\-to` unit pair (`amp`, `db`, `hz`, `oppc`). `\-\-norm` (`amptodB`\*(Aqs `\-n`) only applies to `amp \-> db`.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-from\fR \fI<FROM>\fR
Unit to convert from: `amp`, `db`, `hz`, or `oppc`
.TP
\fB\-\-to\fR \fI<TO>\fR
Unit to convert to: `amp`, `db`, `hz`, or `oppc`
.TP
\fB\-\-norm\fR \fI<NORM>\fR [default: 1]
Normalization amplitude for `amp \-> db`: divides the amplitude by this before converting to decibels. Ignored otherwise
.TP
\fB\-\-value\fR \fI<VALUES>\fR
A value to convert; repeat for more than one
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
